<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  #78: the lock control's SHUT padlock — the state the lock is IN when it is holding
  the window and the stream still.

  AUTHORED HERE, in this repo, for this control. Two reasons, and they are the two
  the ask had to weigh:

   - It is MONOCHROME by construction. The emoji this replaces (U+1F512, and U+1F513
     for the other state) was drawn by the device's COLOUR emoji font, which paints
     its own palette and ignores the TextView's text colour — so the control could
     not be the chrome's cyan. Forcing the text presentation with a variation
     selector (U+FE0E) was checked against this device and is not an option there:
     the pulled fonts show the only font covering U+1F512/U+1F513 is NotoColorEmoji
     (range 1f4ff-1f53d), while the monochrome Noto Sans Symbols subsets stop at
     1F251 / 1F0DF — there is no text-presentation glyph to select.
   - It carries NO LICENCE CONSEQUENCE. This is this repo's own art, like
     R.drawable.logo, and the bundled-licence index (app/licenses/components.tsv,
     verified by :app:verifyLicenseIndex) does not cover res/ at all: it indexes the
     app, the resolved Gradle runtime classpath and the Rust crate closure, and the
     verifier's coverage rule is over the classpath modules. Nothing was taken from
     an icon set, so nothing has to be noticed.

  It is a MASK, deliberately: white fill and stroke and no tint of its own, because
  the caller tints it with the app's chrome cyan (ProtoCameraActivity,
  CHROME_GLYPH_COLOR) so the colour has one home. What is decided here is only the
  SHAPE — and the shape is what tells the two states apart now that the colour is the
  same in both (see proto_ic_lock_open.xml): here BOTH shackle legs reach the body.
  At 24dp the body is 13 x 11 units of a 24-unit box, so the control stays legible at
  the 52dp chrome size it is drawn at.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">

  <!-- The body: x 5.5..18.5, y 10.5..21.5, corners r2. -->
  <path
      android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
      android:pathData="M7.5,10.5 H16.5 A2,2 0 0 1 18.5,12.5 V19.5 A2,2 0 0 1 16.5,21.5 H7.5 A2,2 0 0 1 5.5,19.5 V12.5 A2,2 0 0 1 7.5,10.5 Z"/>

  <!-- The shackle, SHUT: both legs come down to the body's top edge (y 10.5). -->
  <path
      android:fillColor="#00000000"
      android:strokeColor="#FFFFFFFF"
      android:strokeWidth="2"
      android:strokeLineCap="round"
      android:pathData="M8.5,10.5 V8 A3.5,3.5 0 0 1 15.5,8 V10.5"/>
</vector>
